      "problem_formulation": {
        "encoding_method": "QUBO",
        "encoding_details": "Binary asset-holding variables x_{i,d} encode discrete weights ω_i = (1/K) * sum_d 2^d x_{i,d}; additional binary indicator variables z_i enforce cardinality. The total qubits/variables are N(D+1), where D is the bit depth needed for the bounded holding range. For the reported bounded setup, Kmax is the rounded integer 20% of K, with D chosen accordingly.",
        "objective_function": "Index tracking objective with cardinality constraint: minimize sum_t (ω^T r_t - r̂_t)^2 + (1·ω - 1)^2 + (1·z - C)^2 + sum_{i,d} z_i x_{i,d}. The paper also states the cardinality-constrained tracking form arg min_{ω,z} sum_t (ω^T r_t - r̂_t)^2 + (1·ω - 1)^2 + (1·z - C)^2 + sum_{i,d} z_i x_{i,d}.",
        "constraints_handling": "Penalty terms enforce full investment and exact cardinality; indicator-variable interactions z_i x_{i,d} couple asset selection to discrete holdings. The formulation is designed so the cardinality constraint is exactly satisfied in a single optimization.",
        "num_binary_variables": null,
        "problem_hamiltonian": null,
        "num_ancilla_qubits": null
      },
